regex 2026.11.19 (mrab-regex), src/_regex.c, for WebAssembly: five functions get the signatures CPython calls them
with. CPython calls a getter as getter(self, closure) and a METH_NOARGS method as meth(self, NULL); these five were
declared with one parameter and cast to the two-parameter type. Native code never notices the extra argument, but
WebAssembly checks the type of every indirect call and traps ("null function or function signature mismatch"):
Pattern.groupindex, pickling a pattern, Match.capturesdict(), allcaptures() and allspans() all failed. Worth reporting
upstream. Applied by build.sh.

